<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokat is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, in the valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yesilirmak">Yeşilırmak</a>, near the site of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comana-pontica">Comana Pontica</a>. It was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmendids">Danishmendids</a>, then by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum and Mongol governors, and was an important stage on the trade routes across Anatolia. Its Seljuk monuments include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gok-madrasa">Gök Medrese</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokat.jpg" alt="Tokat" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lubunya · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tokat_%C5%9Fehir_panoramas%C4%B1_2012.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
